     A          R HSLIST
     A                                  1  2'Help - Spreadsheets'
     A                                      DSPATR(HI)
     A                                  3  3'Your spreadsheets.  Each has colum-
     A                                      ns A to H and rows 1 to 99.'
     A                                  5  3'Options: 2 opens a sheet, 6 prints-
     A                                       it, 4 deletes it.'
     A                                  6  3'You can also put the cursor on a l-
     A                                      ine and press Enter to pick it.'
     A                                  8  3'F6 creates a new sheet.'
     A                                  9  3'F7 and F8 page backward and forwar-
     A                                      d through a long list.'
     A                                 23  2'Press Enter to return.'
     A                                      COLOR(BLU)
     A          R HSNEW
     A                                  1  2'Help - New spreadsheet'
     A                                      DSPATR(HI)
     A                                  3  3'Give the sheet a short name and a -
     A                                      title, then press Enter.'
     A                                  4  3'The sheet opens straight away.'
     A                                 23  2'Press Enter to return.'
     A                                      COLOR(BLU)
     A          R HSGRID
     A                                  1  2'Help - Spreadsheet'
     A                                      DSPATR(HI)
     A                                  3  3'Type straight into the cells.  Eac-
     A                                      h cell shows eight characters.'
     A                                  5  3'Moving around:  Tab moves to the n-
     A                                      ext cell to the right, and on to th-
     A                                      e'
     A                                  6  3'next row.  Backtab (Shift+Tab) mov-
     A                                      es left.  The arrow keys also work.'
     A                                  7  3'Field Exit clears the rest of a ce-
     A                                      ll and moves on, which is the quick-
     A                                       way'
     A                                  8  3'to type over a number.'
     A                                 10  3'Enter stores everything you typed -
     A                                      and moves down one cell, or right o-
     A                                      ne'
     A                                 11  3'cell.  F10 switches between down a-
     A                                      nd right.  Cursor on a cell + Enter'
     A                                 12  3'makes it the current cell: its row-
     A                                       number and column letter light up.'
     A                                 14  3'Yes, it does math.  Start a cell w-
     A                                      ith = for a formula: =B2*C2+10'
     A                                 15  3'Use + - * / with numbers and cells-
     A                                      .  * and / come before + and -.'
     A                                 16  3'=SUM(B2:B9) =AVG(B2:B9) =MIN(B2:B9-
     A                                      ) =MAX(B2:B9) =COUNT(B2:B9)'
     A                                 18  3'A cell shows the result; the line -
     A                                      below the grid shows the formula.'
     A                                 19  3'For text or a formula longer than -
     A                                      eight characters, use Contents.'
     A                                 20  3'F6 empties the current cell, F9 pr-
     A                                      ints, F11 charts the current column-
     A                                      .'
     A                                 23  2'Press Enter to return.'
     A                                      COLOR(BLU)
     A          R HSCHART
     A                                  1  2'Help - Column chart'
     A                                      DSPATR(HI)
     A                                  3  3'Each bar is one number from the cu-
     A                                      rrent column, top to bottom, up to -
     A                                      15.'
     A                                  4  3'The label is the text in column A -
     A                                      of that row, when there is some.'
     A                                  6  3'Bars are drawn to scale against th-
     A                                      e largest number.  Negative numbers'
     A                                  7  3'are drawn with - instead of #.'
     A                                  9  3'Press Enter to go back to the shee-
     A                                      t.'
     A                                 23  2'Press Enter to return.'
     A                                      COLOR(BLU)
